  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "Three trust levels",
      "items": [
        "Tailscale proves the device; SIGHTR_TRUSTED_USER must match the injected login",
        "The bridge refuses a non-loopback bind, and drops non-loopback peers before routing",
        "Host allowlist precedes Origin; a write also needs an allowlisted device header"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "One socket adapter",
      "items": [
        "herdr-client.ts is the only file that knows Herdr's method names",
        "Each RPC opens a connection, reads one line, closes — a named pipe on Windows",
        "A reply is send_text, a 350 ms settle, then send_keys; the queue 503s after 10 s"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "Events are only a poke",
      "items": [
        "events.subscribe re-polls at once; session.snapshot stays the source of truth",
        "SSE coalesces 250 ms and returns over the same tailnet HTTPS connection",
        "sightr @ b530f34 — env identifiers are still spelled SIGHTR_ in the code"
      ]
    }
  ]
